cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "GeoCamPal"
abstract: >-
  Camera-derived imagery is increasingly used across environmental monitoring
  programmes for geospatial analysis, but reproducible image-processing
  workflows often remain fragmented across programming languages, proprietary
  platforms, and single-purpose scripts. GeoCamPal is an open-source,
  Python-based graphical toolbox for camera-derived geospatial image analysis.
  Built on OpenCV, GDAL/Rasterio, GeoPandas/Shapely, NumPy/SciPy/Pandas,
  Matplotlib, and CustomTkinter, it combines field-of-view visualisation,
  lens-distortion correction, image-quality filtering, brightness and colour
  harmonisation, multi-method georeferencing, feature identification,
  machine-learning training-data labelling, event-based image selection,
  colour-space analysis, and reproducible batch processing in a single
  interface. The software also provides specialised coastal-monitoring
  workflows, including support for shoreline extraction, timestack generation,
  wave run-up analysis, and waterline-based digital elevation model
  construction. GeoCamPal reduces workflow fragmentation and lowers technical
  barriers to reproducible camera-derived environmental analysis. The workflow
  is developed and shown for coastal beach camera analyses, but may be used
  for other applications.
